---
// Flagship B — page anatomy per spec §B5: constellation hero → 4 chapters →
// explore → methodology. Identity: smelter metal (spec §B6).
// Product space renders in 3-D (Three.js); the third axis can be the force
// layout's depth or the product's complexity (PCI) — "altitude".
import "../styles/tokens.css";
const summary = (await import("../data/summary.json").catch(() => null))?.default ?? {
  latestYear: 2024, totalExports: 0, idnRank: {}, nCountries: 0, peers: [] };
const latest = summary.latestYear;
const rankNow = summary.idnRank?.[String(latest)] ?? "—";
const rankThen = summary.idnRank?.[String(latest - 10)] ?? "—";
const exportsB = summary.totalExports ? Math.round(summary.totalExports / 1e6) : null;
---
<html lang="en" data-case="trade" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Indonesia in the Global Trade Network</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=Public+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="stamp-bar">
      <span class="stamp">INDONESIA IN THE GLOBAL TRADE NETWORK</span>
      <span class="stamp dim">BACI 202601 · TRADE DATA THROUGH {latest} · GOODS ONLY</span>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <canvas id="hero-canvas"></canvas>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Every product the world trades — and where Indonesia stands among them.</h1>
        <p>{summary.nCountries ? `${summary.nCountries} economies` : "The world"}, ~1,200 products, thirty years of
        bilateral trade, distilled into one map. Copper marks what Indonesia exports
        competitively.</p>
        <span class="stamp dim" id="hero-status">ASSEMBLING THE PRODUCT SPACE…</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 · The basket</span>
      <h2>What Indonesia sells the world</h2>
      <p>Export shares by product chapter. Scrub the years: watch oil, gas, and wood give
      way to palm and coal — then the nickel complex bloom.</p>
      <div class="scrub"><span class="stamp dim">YEAR</span>
        <input type="range" id="tm-year" min="1995" max={latest} value={latest} />
        <span class="stamp" id="tm-label">{latest}</span></div>
      <div id="treemap" class="chart tall"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · The gambit</span>
      <h2>The nickel gambit</h2>
      <p>Indonesia banned raw nickel-ore exports in 2014, relaxed the ban, then closed it
      for good in 2020. Ore exports collapsed; processed nickel — ferroalloys, mattes,
      stainless — surged. That part of the story is true, and here it is in the data.</p>
      <div id="nickel" class="chart"></div>
      <p class="footnote">Values in current US$; HS92 codes 2604 (ore) vs 7202, 7501–7503,
      7218–7220 (processed). Source: BACI.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">03 · The paradox</span>
      <h2>More value, same place — while the neighbors climbed</h2>
      <p class="big-stat">Indonesia ranks <b class="copper">#{rankNow}</b> in economic complexity
      in {latest} — versus <b class="copper">#{rankThen}</b> a decade earlier. Fifteen times
      the processed-nickel exports; a rank that barely moved.</p>
      <p>Complexity rewards the diversity and sophistication of the whole export basket.
      Downstreaming multiplied the value of one chapter, but a single-commodity climb does
      not diversify a basket — so Indonesia held its place in the mid-seventies while
      Vietnam, the Philippines, and India each climbed twenty or more places over the same
      decade. Every line here is computed from the same corpus; our 2023 rank (#71 of 158)
      lands within three places of Harvard’s Atlas (#69 of 133) — the independent check the
      methodology footer describes.</p>
      <div id="trajectory" class="chart"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">04 · What’s adjacent</span>
      <h2>The nearest steps not yet taken</h2>
      <p>Products Indonesia does not yet export competitively, placed by how close they sit
      to what it already makes (density) and how sophisticated they are (PCI). The
      upper-right corner is the strategic frontier.</p>
      <div id="adjacency" class="chart"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="explore">
      <div class="explore-head">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">05 · Explore</span><h2>The product space, in three dimensions</h2></div>
        <div class="controls">
          <label class="stamp dim">YEAR <input type="range" id="ps-year" min="1995" max={latest} value={latest} /> <span id="ps-label" class="stamp">{latest}</span></label>
          <div class="toggle" role="group" aria-label="third axis">
            <button id="alt-net" class="on">DEPTH: NETWORK</button><button id="alt-pci">ALTITUDE: PCI</button>
          </div>
          <div class="search-wrap">
            <input id="ps-search" type="search" placeholder="Search a product — any language…" autocomplete="off" />
            <div id="ps-results" hidden></div>
            <span id="search-status" class="stamp dim"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-wrap">
        <canvas id="ps-canvas"></canvas>
        <div id="ps-tip" hidden></div>
        <div class="legend stamp dim">● COPPER — INDONESIA EXPORTS WITH COMPARATIVE ADVANTAGE &nbsp; ● SILVER — WORLD STRUCTURE &nbsp; · DRAG TO ORBIT · SCROLL TO ZOOM</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="method">
      <span class="eyebrow">Methodology &amp; sources</span>
      <p>Flows: CEPII BACI release 202601 (HS92, 1995–{latest}, Etalab 2.0 licence), ~330M
      rows in DuckDB. Sample: economies with population ≥ 1M (World Bank) and total trade
      ≥ US$1B per year — the Atlas rules. Complexity: Balassa RCA → M matrix (RCA ≥ 1) →
      ECI/PCI via Harvard Growth Lab’s <code>py-ecomplexity</code> at HS4, PCI sign normalized
      to Atlas convention (no year required flipping). Product space: maximum-spanning-tree
      backbone + proximity ≥ 0.55, seeded 3-D force layout computed once; the “altitude”
      view replaces layout depth with PCI. Product search is lexical over every HS6
      description (prefix and one-edit fuzzy matching) plus semantic: each product’s
      descriptions are embedded with a locally hosted multilingual-E5 model served by the
      lab’s own embedding endpoint, so a query in Bahasa Indonesia finds English product
      names — the same local-embedding capability that powers Pustaka. (A fully static
      alternative would run the encoder in-browser with transformers.js, at the cost of a
      30–100 MB first-visit download.) <b>Caveats stated plainly:</b> goods only; the
      log-supermodularity condition — Growth Lab’s structural-ranking check — holds for
      roughly a third of country-product pairs in early years, so ECI is a ranking, not a
      cardinal measure. <b>Gate G-B1:</b> Indonesia 2023 rank #71 of 158 here vs #69 of 133 in
      the Atlas — within three places.</p>
      <span class="stamp dim">A DEMO-LAB CASE · ANNUAL REBUILD · {exportsB ? `IDN GOODS EXPORTS ${latest}: US$${exportsB}B` : ""}</span>
    </footer>
    <div id="chart-tip" hidden></div>

    <script>
      import * as d3 from "d3";
      import * as THREE from "three";
      import { OrbitControls } from "three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js";

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const COPPER = "#D9722C", SILVER = "#AEB6C2", VERDIGRIS = "#58A89B", INK = "#0C0F14";
      const SECTORS = [ // [maxHS2, label, color] — desaturated for the dark ground
        [5, "Animal", "#8C7A6B"], [15, "Vegetable & fats", "#7E9A6C"], [24, "Foodstuffs", "#A48E5A"],
        [27, "Minerals & fuels", "#6E7887"], [38, "Chemicals", "#7D6F9C"], [40, "Plastics & rubber", "#6C8FA1"],
        [43, "Hides", "#8D7355"], [49, "Wood & paper", "#7C8A61"], [63, "Textiles", "#9A6F86"],
        [67, "Footwear", "#8F7D9A"], [71, "Stone, glass, gems", "#6F97A6"], [83, "Metals", "#9AA3AF"],
        [85, "Machinery & electrical", "#5D8FBF"], [89, "Transport", "#5FA8B5"], [99, "Instruments & misc", "#B0A46B"],
      ];
      const sectorOf = (hs2) => SECTORS.find(([max]) => +hs2 <= max);
      const reduced = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
      const load = (f) => fetch(`${base}/data/${f}`).then((r) => { if (!r.ok) throw f; return r.json(); });

      let space, names, states, treemap, traj, nickel, adjacency;
      try {
        [space, names, states, treemap, traj, nickel, adjacency] = await Promise.all(
          ["product_space.json", "names.json", "space_states.json", "treemap.json",
           "trajectory.json", "nickel.json", "adjacency.json"].map(load));
      } catch (missing) {
        document.getElementById("hero-status").textContent =
          `PIPELINE STILL RUNNING — ${missing} not yet exported. Refresh in a few minutes.`;
        throw missing;
      }
      const latest = String(space.year);
      const label = (id) => names[id] ?? `HS ${id}`;

      /* shared chart tooltip + end-label de-collision */
      const ctip = document.getElementById("chart-tip");
      const showTip = (e, html) => { ctip.hidden = false; ctip.innerHTML = html; ctip.style.left = e.pageX + 14 + "px"; ctip.style.top = e.pageY + 14 + "px"; };
      const hideTip = () => { ctip.hidden = true; };
      const fmt$ = (v) => "$" + d3.format(".3s")(v).replace("G", "B");
      function spread(items, minGap, lo, hi) {
        items.sort((a, b) => a.y - b.y);
        for (let i = 1; i < items.length; i++) if (items[i].y - items[i - 1].y < minGap) items[i].y = items[i - 1].y + minGap;
        const over = items.at(-1).y - hi;
        if (over > 0) for (const it of items) it.y -= over;
        for (let i = items.length - 2; i >= 0; i--) if (items[i + 1].y - items[i].y < minGap) items[i].y = items[i + 1].y - minGap;
        if (items[0].y < lo) { const up = lo - items[0].y; for (const it of items) it.y += up; }
        return items;
      }

      /* ---------- 3-D product space (shared by hero + explore) ---------- */
      const SPAN = 120;
      const ext = (k) => d3.extent(space.nodes, (n) => n[k] ?? 0);
      const sx = d3.scaleLinear(ext("x"), [-SPAN, SPAN]);
      const sy = d3.scaleLinear(ext("y"), [-SPAN, SPAN]);
      const sz = d3.scaleLinear(ext("z"), [-SPAN, SPAN]);
      const spci = d3.scaleLinear(ext("pci"), [-SPAN * 0.7, SPAN * 0.7]);
      const rScale = d3.scaleSqrt(d3.extent(space.nodes, (n) => n.trade), [2.2, 11]);
      // hero reveal order: by sector, then trade — nodes stream in sector by sector
      const order = [...space.nodes].sort((a, b) =>
        sectorOf(a.hs2)[1].localeCompare(sectorOf(b.hs2)[1]) || a.trade - b.trade);
      const indexOf = new Map(order.map((n, i) => [n.id, i]));

      const POINT_VS = `
        attribute float size; attribute vec3 color; attribute float alpha;
        varying vec3 vColor; varying float vAlpha;
        void main() {
          vColor = color; vAlpha = alpha;
          vec4 mv = modelViewMatrix * vec4(position, 1.0);
          gl_PointSize = size * (420.0 / -mv.z);
          gl_Position = projectionMatrix * mv;
        }`;
      const POINT_FS = `
        varying vec3 vColor; varying float vAlpha;
        void main() {
          float d = length(gl_PointCoord - 0.5);
          if (d > 0.5) discard;
          float edge = smoothstep(0.5, 0.36, d);
          gl_FragColor = vec4(vColor, vAlpha * edge);
        }`;

      function makeSpace(canvas, { interactive }) {
        const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ canvas, antialias: true, alpha: false });
        renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));
        renderer.setClearColor(new THREE.Color(INK), 1);
        const scene = new THREE.Scene();
        scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(new THREE.Color(INK), SPAN * 1.6, SPAN * 5);
        const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(48, 1, 1, 4000);
        camera.position.set(0, SPAN * 0.35, SPAN * 2.6);
        const controls = new OrbitControls(camera, canvas);
        controls.enableDamping = true; controls.dampingFactor = 0.06;
        controls.enablePan = false; controls.minDistance = SPAN * 0.6; controls.maxDistance = SPAN * 5;
        controls.autoRotate = !reduced; controls.autoRotateSpeed = interactive ? 0.25 : 0.55;
        controls.enabled = interactive;

        const n = order.length;
        const pos = new Float32Array(n * 3), col = new Float32Array(n * 3);
        const size = new Float32Array(n), alpha = new Float32Array(n);
        const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        geo.setAttribute("position", new THREE.BufferAttribute(pos, 3));
        geo.setAttribute("color", new THREE.BufferAttribute(col, 3));
        geo.setAttribute("size", new THREE.BufferAttribute(size, 1));
        geo.setAttribute("alpha", new THREE.BufferAttribute(alpha, 1));
        const pts = new THREE.Points(geo, new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
          vertexShader: POINT_VS, fragmentShader: POINT_FS, transparent: true, depthWrite: false }));
        scene.add(pts);
        // copper glow layer: same positions, only lit nodes visible, additive
        const gsize = new Float32Array(n), galpha = new Float32Array(n), gcol = new Float32Array(n * 3);
        const ggeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        ggeo.setAttribute("position", new THREE.BufferAttribute(pos, 3));
        ggeo.setAttribute("color", new THREE.BufferAttribute(gcol, 3));
        ggeo.setAttribute("size", new THREE.BufferAttribute(gsize, 1));
        ggeo.setAttribute("alpha", new THREE.BufferAttribute(galpha, 1));
        const glow = new THREE.Points(ggeo, new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
          vertexShader: POINT_VS, fragmentShader: POINT_FS, transparent: true, depthWrite: false,
          blending: THREE.AdditiveBlending }));
        scene.add(glow);
        // edges
        const idIndex = new Map(space.nodes.map((nd) => [nd.id, nd]));
        const epos = new Float32Array(space.edges.length * 6);
        const egeo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();
        egeo.setAttribute("position", new THREE.BufferAttribute(epos, 3));
        const edges = new THREE.LineSegments(egeo, new THREE.LineBasicMaterial({
          color: new THREE.Color(SILVER), transparent: true, opacity: 0.16, depthWrite: false }));
        scene.add(edges);
        // hover ring
        const ring = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.RingGeometry(1, 1.25, 40),
          new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: "#E6E8EC", side: THREE.DoubleSide, transparent: true, opacity: 0.9 }));
        ring.visible = false; scene.add(ring);

        let mode = "net", lit = new Set(states[latest] ?? []), filter = null, progress = 1;
        const copper = new THREE.Color(COPPER);
        const zOf = (nd) => mode === "pci" ? spci(nd.pci) : sz(nd.z ?? 0);

        function layoutPositions() {
          order.forEach((nd, i) => { pos[i * 3] = sx(nd.x); pos[i * 3 + 1] = zOf(nd); pos[i * 3 + 2] = sy(nd.y); });
          geo.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true; ggeo.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;
          space.edges.forEach(([a, b], k) => {
            const na = idIndex.get(a), nb = idIndex.get(b);
            if (!na || !nb) return;
            epos.set([sx(na.x), zOf(na), sy(na.y), sx(nb.x), zOf(nb), sy(nb.y)], k * 6);
          });
          egeo.attributes.position.needsUpdate = true;
          geo.computeBoundingSphere();
        }
        function paint() {
          order.forEach((nd, i) => {
            const isLit = lit.has(nd.id), dim = filter && !filter.has(nd.id);
            const c = isLit ? copper : new THREE.Color(sectorOf(nd.hs2)[2]);
            col.set([c.r, c.g, c.b], i * 3);
            size[i] = rScale(nd.trade) * (isLit ? 1.15 : 1);
            alpha[i] = dim ? 0.08 : isLit ? 0.98 : 0.62;
            gcol.set([copper.r, copper.g, copper.b], i * 3);
            gsize[i] = rScale(nd.trade) * 3.2;
            galpha[i] = isLit && !dim ? 0.22 : 0;
          });
          geo.attributes.color.needsUpdate = geo.attributes.size.needsUpdate = geo.attributes.alpha.needsUpdate = true;
          ggeo.attributes.color.needsUpdate = ggeo.attributes.size.needsUpdate = ggeo.attributes.alpha.needsUpdate = true;
        }
        function reveal() {
          const shown = Math.floor(n * Math.min(progress, 1));
          geo.setDrawRange(0, shown); ggeo.setDrawRange(0, shown);
          edges.material.opacity = progress > 0.7 ? 0.16 * Math.min((progress - 0.7) / 0.3, 1) : 0;
        }
        function size2() {
          const W = canvas.clientWidth, H = canvas.clientHeight;
          renderer.setSize(W, H, false); camera.aspect = W / H; camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
        }
        size2(); addEventListener("resize", size2);
        layoutPositions(); paint(); reveal();

        if (interactive) {
          const tip = document.getElementById("ps-tip");
          const ray = new THREE.Raycaster(); ray.params.Points.threshold = 3.2;
          const mouse = new THREE.Vector2();
          let hovered = null;
          canvas.addEventListener("mousemove", (e) => {
            const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
            mouse.set(((e.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1, -((e.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1);
            ray.setFromCamera(mouse, camera);
            const hit = ray.intersectObject(pts, false).sort((a, b) => a.distanceToRay - b.distanceToRay)[0];
            if (hit && alpha[hit.index] > 0.2) {
              const nd = order[hit.index]; hovered = nd;
              ring.visible = true; ring.position.set(pos[hit.index * 3], pos[hit.index * 3 + 1], pos[hit.index * 3 + 2]);
              ring.scale.setScalar(rScale(nd.trade) * 0.55 + 1.2); ring.lookAt(camera.position);
              tip.hidden = false; tip.style.left = e.clientX - rect.left + 14 + "px"; tip.style.top = e.clientY - rect.top + 14 + "px";
              tip.innerHTML = `<b>${label(nd.id)}</b><br>HS ${nd.id} · ${sectorOf(nd.hs2)[1]}<br>PCI ${nd.pci.toFixed(2)} · world trade $${d3.format(".3s")(nd.trade * 1e3)}<br>${lit.has(nd.id) ? "<span class='copper'>● Indonesia exports competitively</span>" : "<span class='dim'>○ not yet an Indonesian strength</span>"}`;
            } else { hovered = null; ring.visible = false; tip.hidden = true; }
          });
          canvas.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => { ring.visible = false; tip.hidden = true; });
          canvas.addEventListener("pointerdown", () => { controls.autoRotate = false; });
        }

        let running = true;
        const io = new IntersectionObserver(([en]) => { running = en.isIntersecting; }, { threshold: 0.05 });
        io.observe(canvas);
        function frame() {
          requestAnimationFrame(frame);
          if (!running) return;
          controls.update();
          if (ring.visible) ring.lookAt(camera.position);
          renderer.render(scene, camera);
        }
        frame();

        return {
          setYear(yr) { lit = new Set(states[String(yr)] ?? []); paint(); },
          setFilter(ids) { filter = ids && ids.size ? ids : null; paint(); },
          setMode(m) { mode = m; layoutPositions(); },
          focus(id) {
            const i = indexOf.get(id); if (i == null) return;
            const p = new THREE.Vector3(pos[i * 3], pos[i * 3 + 1], pos[i * 3 + 2]);
            controls.autoRotate = false;
            const dir = camera.position.clone().sub(controls.target).normalize();
            controls.target.copy(p);
            camera.position.copy(p.clone().add(dir.multiplyScalar(SPAN * 0.9)));
            ring.visible = true; ring.position.copy(p); ring.scale.setScalar(rScale(order[i].trade) * 0.55 + 1.2);
          },
          animate(ms) {
            if (reduced) { progress = 1; reveal(); return; }
            progress = 0; reveal();
            const t0 = performance.now();
            const step = (t) => {
              progress = Math.min((t - t0) / ms, 1); reveal();
              if (progress < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);
              else document.getElementById("hero-status").textContent =
                `${space.nodes.length} PRODUCTS · ${space.edges.length} LINKS · ${lit.size} INDONESIAN STRENGTHS IN ${latest} · 3-D FORCE LAYOUT`;
            };
            requestAnimationFrame(step);
          },
        };
      }
      const hero = makeSpace(document.getElementById("hero-canvas"), { interactive: false });
      hero.animate(4600);
      const explore = makeSpace(document.getElementById("ps-canvas"), { interactive: true });
      document.getElementById("ps-year").addEventListener("input", (e) => { explore.setYear(e.target.value); document.getElementById("ps-label").textContent = e.target.value; });
      /* ---------- product search: lexical (all HS6 descriptions, prefix + fuzzy) first,
         semantic (local multilingual-E5 via the lab's embedding service) layered on top.
         Alternative for a fully static deploy: run the encoder in-browser with
         transformers.js — same vectors, but a 30–100 MB model download on first visit. */
      const EMBED_API = "http://localhost:8600/api/embed"; // TODO prod: /knowledge/api/embed
      const [searchText, vectors] = await Promise.all([
        load("search_text.json").catch(() => null), load("product_vectors.json").catch(() => null)]);
      const tokenize = (s) => s.toLowerCase().normalize("NFKD").replace(/[^\p{L}\p{N}\s]/gu, " ").split(/\s+/).filter((t) => t.length > 1);
      const lex = space.nodes.map((nd) => {
        const text = ((searchText?.[nd.id] ?? label(nd.id)) + " " + label(nd.id)).toLowerCase();
        return { id: nd.id, text, tokens: new Set(tokenize(text)) };
      });
      const editDistance1 = (a, b) => { // Damerau-lite: one edit or one transposition
        if (Math.abs(a.length - b.length) > 1) return false;
        let i = 0, j = 0, edits = 0;
        while (i < a.length && j < b.length) {
          if (a[i] === b[j]) { i++; j++; continue; }
          if (++edits > 1) return false;
          if (a.length > b.length) i++; else if (b.length > a.length) j++;
          else if (a[i + 1] === b[j] && a[i] === b[j + 1]) { i += 2; j += 2; } else { i++; j++; }
        }
        return edits + (a.length - i) + (b.length - j) <= 1;
      };
      // Bahasa ↔ English trade glossary: deterministic hits for the common terms,
      // independent of embedding quality. Expand each query token with its synonyms.
      const GLOSSARY = {
        sawit: ["palm"], "kelapa sawit": ["palm"], minyak: ["oil", "oils"], mobil: ["motor", "vehicles", "cars"],
        kendaraan: ["vehicles"], kopi: ["coffee"], nikel: ["nickel"], bijih: ["ores", "ore"], batubara: ["coal"],
        batu: ["stone"], karet: ["rubber"], kayu: ["wood"], kertas: ["paper"], pakaian: ["apparel", "garments", "clothing"],
        baju: ["apparel", "garments"], sepatu: ["footwear", "shoes"], tekstil: ["textile", "textiles"], ikan: ["fish"],
        udang: ["shrimps", "prawns"], tembaga: ["copper"], emas: ["gold"], timah: ["tin"], baja: ["steel"], besi: ["iron"],
        pupuk: ["fertilisers", "fertilizers"], gas: ["gas"], alam: ["natural"], kakao: ["cocoa"], coklat: ["chocolate", "cocoa"],
        teh: ["tea"], gula: ["sugar"], beras: ["rice"], padi: ["rice"], jagung: ["maize", "corn"], kedelai: ["soya"],
        obat: ["medicaments", "pharmaceutical"], mesin: ["machinery", "machines"], listrik: ["electric", "electrical"],
        elektronik: ["electronic"], komputer: ["computers", "data processing"], ponsel: ["telephones"], kapal: ["ships", "vessels"],
        pesawat: ["aircraft"], semen: ["cement"], plastik: ["plastics"], kaca: ["glass"], kulit: ["leather", "hides"],
        perhiasan: ["jewellery"], furnitur: ["furniture"], mebel: ["furniture"], rokok: ["cigarettes", "tobacco"], tembakau: ["tobacco"],
        aluminium: ["aluminium"], alumunium: ["aluminium"], kimia: ["chemical", "chemicals"], cat: ["paints"], ban: ["tyres"],
      };
      const expand = (tokens) => tokens.flatMap((t) => [t, ...(GLOSSARY[t] ?? [])]);
      function lexicalMatch(q) {
        const raw = tokenize(q);
        if (!raw.length) return [];
        // a query token matches if it OR any of its glossary synonyms match
        const groups = raw.map((t) => expand([t]));
        const hits = [];
        for (const p of lex) {
          let score = 0;
          if (p.id.startsWith(q.replace(/\D/g, "")) && /^\d{2,4}$/.test(q)) score += 3;
          for (const g of groups) {
            let best = 0;
            for (const t of g) {
              let s = 0;
              if (p.tokens.has(t)) s = 2;
              else if (t.length >= 3 && [...p.tokens].some((k) => k.startsWith(t))) s = 1.2;
              else if (t.length >= 5 && [...p.tokens].some((k) => editDistance1(k, t))) s = 0.8;
              else if (p.text.includes(t)) s = 0.6;
              if (s > best) best = s;
            }
            if (!best) { score = 0; break; } // every query token (or a synonym) must match
            score += best;
          }
          if (score > 0) hits.push({ id: p.id, score, how: "lexical" });
        }
        return hits.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);
      }
      let vecStore = null;
      if (vectors) {
        const raw = Uint8Array.from(atob(vectors.q), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0));
        vecStore = { dims: vectors.dims, ids: vectors.ids, scale: vectors.scale, q: new Int8Array(raw.buffer) };
      }
      async function semanticMatch(q) {
        if (!vecStore) return { hits: [], reason: "no vectors" };
        const res = await fetch(EMBED_API, { method: "POST", headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
          body: JSON.stringify({ texts: [q], kind: "query" }) }).then((r) => r.json());
        const qv = res.vectors[0];
        const { dims, ids, scale, q: qs } = vecStore;
        const sims = ids.map((id, r) => {
          let dot = 0; const off = r * dims, k = scale[r] / 127;
          for (let d = 0; d < dims; d++) dot += qs[off + d] * qv[d];
          return { id, sim: dot * k };
        }).sort((a, b) => b.sim - a.sim);
        const top = sims[0].sim;
        return { hits: sims.slice(0, 40).filter((s) => s.sim >= top - 0.05).map((s) => ({ id: s.id, score: s.sim, how: "semantic" })) };
      }
      const resultsEl = document.getElementById("ps-results"), statusEl = document.getElementById("search-status");
      let searchSeq = 0;
      async function runSearch(q) {
        q = q.trim();
        if (!q) { explore.setFilter(null); resultsEl.hidden = true; statusEl.textContent = ""; return; }
        const seq = ++searchSeq;
        const lexHits = lexicalMatch(q.toLowerCase());
        const show = (hits, note) => {
          if (seq !== searchSeq) return;
          const seen = new Set(); const merged = hits.filter((h) => !seen.has(h.id) && seen.add(h.id));
          explore.setFilter(new Set(merged.map((h) => h.id)));
          resultsEl.hidden = merged.length === 0;
          resultsEl.innerHTML = merged.slice(0, 8).map((h) =>
            `<button type="button" data-id="${h.id}"><span>${label(h.id)}</span><i>HS ${h.id} · ${h.how}</i></button>`).join("");
          resultsEl.querySelectorAll("button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
            explore.focus(b.dataset.id); document.getElementById("ps-year").scrollIntoView({ block: "nearest" }); }));
          statusEl.textContent = `${merged.length} MATCH${merged.length === 1 ? "" : "ES"} · ${note}`;
        };
        show(lexHits, vecStore ? "LEXICAL · SEMANTIC PENDING…" : "LEXICAL ONLY");
        if (!vecStore) return;
        try {
          const sem = await semanticMatch(q);
          show([...lexHits, ...sem.hits], "LEXICAL + SEMANTIC (MULTILINGUAL-E5, LOCAL)");
        } catch {
          show(lexHits, "LEXICAL ONLY — EMBEDDING SERVICE OFFLINE");
        }
      }
      let debounce;
      document.getElementById("ps-search").addEventListener("input", (e) => {
        clearTimeout(debounce); debounce = setTimeout(() => runSearch(e.target.value), 220);
      });
      const bNet = document.getElementById("alt-net"), bPci = document.getElementById("alt-pci");
      const setMode = (m) => { explore.setMode(m); bNet.classList.toggle("on", m === "net"); bPci.classList.toggle("on", m === "pci"); };
      bNet.onclick = () => setMode("net"); bPci.onclick = () => setMode("pci");

      /* ---------- chapter 1: treemap ---------- */
      {
        const el = document.getElementById("treemap");
        const W = el.clientWidth, H = 380;
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        const color = (hs2) => sectorOf(hs2)[2];
        function render(year) {
          const rows = (treemap[String(year)] ?? []).slice(0, 18);
          const root = d3.hierarchy({ children: rows }).sum((d) => d.v);
          d3.treemap().size([W, H]).paddingInner(2)(root);
          const total = d3.sum(rows, (d) => d.v);
          const g = svg.selectAll("g.cell").data(root.leaves(), (d) => d.data.hs2)
            .join((enter) => { const g = enter.append("g").attr("class", "cell"); g.append("rect"); g.append("text").attr("class", "tm-name"); g.append("text").attr("class", "tm-pct"); return g; });
          g.on("mousemove", (e, d) => showTip(e, `<b>${d.data.name}</b><br>HS ${d.data.hs2} · ${fmt$(d.data.v * 1e3)}<br>${d3.format(".1%")(d.data.v / total)} of ${year} exports`))
           .on("mouseleave", hideTip);
          g.transition().duration(reduced ? 0 : 500).attr("transform", (d) => `translate(${d.x0},${d.y0})`);
          g.select("rect").transition().duration(reduced ? 0 : 500).attr("width", (d) => d.x1 - d.x0).attr("height", (d) => d.y1 - d.y0)
            .attr("fill", (d) => ["26", "72", "75"].includes(d.data.hs2) ? COPPER : color(d.data.hs2)).attr("opacity", 0.8);
          g.select(".tm-name").attr("x", 6).attr("y", 16).text((d) => (d.x1 - d.x0 > 70 && d.y1 - d.y0 > 30) ? d.data.name : "");
          g.select(".tm-pct").attr("x", 6).attr("y", 30).text((d) => (d.x1 - d.x0 > 70 && d.y1 - d.y0 > 44) ? d3.format(".0%")(d.data.v / total) : "");
        }
        render(latest);
        document.getElementById("tm-year").addEventListener("input", (e) => { render(e.target.value); document.getElementById("tm-label").textContent = e.target.value; });
      }

      /* ---------- chapter 2: nickel ---------- */
      {
        const el = document.getElementById("nickel");
        const W = el.clientWidth, H = 280, M = { t: 20, r: 20, b: 30, l: 60 };
        const years = Object.keys(nickel.ore).map(Number).sort();
        const series = (obj) => years.map((yr) => ({ yr, v: (obj[String(yr)] ?? 0) * 1e3 }));
        const ore = series(nickel.ore), proc = series(nickel.processed);
        const x = d3.scaleLinear(d3.extent(years), [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max([...ore, ...proc], (d) => d.v) * 1.08], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(4).tickFormat((v) => "$" + d3.format("~s")(v)));
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x).tickFormat(d3.format("d")));
        for (const [yr, txt] of [[2014, "first ore ban"], [2020, "full ban"]]) {
          svg.append("line").attr("x1", x(yr)).attr("x2", x(yr)).attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", "#3A4452").attr("stroke-dasharray", "3 4");
          svg.append("text").attr("x", x(yr) + 5).attr("y", M.t + 10).attr("class", "annot").text(`${yr} · ${txt}`);
        }
        const line = d3.line().x((d) => x(d.yr)).y((d) => y(d.v)).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        svg.append("path").datum(ore).attr("d", line).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", SILVER).attr("stroke-width", 1.8);
        svg.append("path").datum(proc).attr("d", line).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", COPPER).attr("stroke-width", 2.2);
        const labels = spread([
          { y: y(ore.at(-1).v), text: "ore (HS 2604)", fill: SILVER },
          { y: y(proc.at(-1).v), text: "processed nickel & stainless", fill: COPPER }], 14, M.t + 8, H - M.b - 4);
        svg.selectAll("text.end").data(labels).join("text").attr("class", "annot end")
          .attr("x", W - M.r).attr("y", (d) => d.y - 6).attr("text-anchor", "end").attr("fill", (d) => d.fill).text((d) => d.text);
        // hover: crosshair + dots + tooltip
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", "#E6E8EC").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.45).style("display", "none");
        const dots = svg.selectAll("circle.h").data([ore, proc]).join("circle").attr("class", "h").attr("r", 4)
          .attr("fill", (d, i) => (i ? COPPER : SILVER)).attr("stroke", INK).style("display", "none");
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b).attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const yr = Math.round(x.invert(d3.pointer(e)[0])); const i = years.indexOf(yr); if (i < 0) return;
            guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(yr)).attr("x2", x(yr));
            dots.style("display", null).attr("cx", x(yr)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d[i].v));
            showTip(e, `<b>${yr}</b><br><span style="color:${COPPER}">●</span> processed ${fmt$(proc[i].v)}<br><span style="color:${SILVER}">●</span> ore ${fmt$(ore[i].v)}`);
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { guide.style("display", "none"); dots.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); });
      }

      /* ---------- chapter 3: trajectory ---------- */
      {
        const el = document.getElementById("trajectory");
        const W = el.clientWidth, H = 300, M = { t: 16, r: 60, b: 30, l: 44 };
        const years = Object.keys(traj.ranks.IDN).map(Number).sort();
        const maxRank = d3.max(Object.values(traj.ranks).flatMap((r) => Object.values(r)));
        const x = d3.scaleLinear(d3.extent(years), [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([1, maxRank], [M.t, H - M.b]);
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(5).tickFormat((v) => "#" + v));
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x).tickFormat(d3.format("d")));
        const line = d3.line().defined((d) => d.r != null).x((d) => x(d.yr)).y((d) => y(d.r)).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        const series = Object.entries(traj.ranks).map(([iso, ranks]) => ({
          iso, isIdn: iso === "IDN", pts: years.map((yr) => ({ yr, r: ranks[String(yr)] ?? null })) }));
        const paths = svg.selectAll("path.s").data(series).join("path").attr("class", "s")
          .attr("d", (s) => line(s.pts)).attr("fill", "none")
          .attr("stroke", (s) => (s.isIdn ? COPPER : VERDIGRIS)).attr("stroke-width", (s) => (s.isIdn ? 2.6 : 1.2))
          .attr("opacity", (s) => (s.isIdn ? 1 : 0.7));
        const labels = spread(series.map((s) => {
          const last = s.pts.filter((d) => d.r != null).at(-1);
          return { y: y(last.r), text: `${s.iso} #${last.r}`, fill: s.isIdn ? COPPER : VERDIGRIS, iso: s.iso, x: x(last.yr) };
        }), 13, M.t + 4, H - M.b - 2);
        svg.selectAll("text.end").data(labels).join("text").attr("class", "annot end")
          .attr("x", (d) => d.x + 8).attr("y", (d) => d.y + 4).attr("fill", (d) => d.fill).text((d) => d.text);
        // hover: crosshair + per-series dots + ranked tooltip; hovering a label highlights its line
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", "#E6E8EC").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.45).style("display", "none");
        const dots = svg.selectAll("circle.h").data(series).join("circle").attr("class", "h").attr("r", 3.5)
          .attr("fill", (s) => (s.isIdn ? COPPER : VERDIGRIS)).attr("stroke", INK).style("display", "none");
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b).attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const yr = Math.round(x.invert(d3.pointer(e)[0])); const i = years.indexOf(yr); if (i < 0) return;
            guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(yr)).attr("x2", x(yr));
            dots.style("display", (s) => (s.pts[i].r == null ? "none" : null)).attr("cx", x(yr)).attr("cy", (s) => y(s.pts[i].r ?? 1));
            const rows = series.filter((s) => s.pts[i].r != null).sort((a, b) => a.pts[i].r - b.pts[i].r)
              .map((s) => `<span style="color:${s.isIdn ? COPPER : VERDIGRIS}">${s.isIdn ? "<b>" : ""}${s.iso} #${s.pts[i].r}${s.isIdn ? "</b>" : ""}</span>`);
            showTip(e, `<b>${yr}</b> · ECI rank<br>${rows.join("<br>")}`);
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { guide.style("display", "none"); dots.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); });
        svg.selectAll("text.end").style("cursor", "default")
          .on("mouseenter", (e, d) => paths.attr("opacity", (s) => (s.iso === d.iso ? 1 : 0.15)).attr("stroke-width", (s) => (s.iso === d.iso ? 2.6 : 1.2)))
          .on("mouseleave", () => paths.attr("opacity", (s) => (s.isIdn ? 1 : 0.7)).attr("stroke-width", (s) => (s.isIdn ? 2.6 : 1.2)));
      }

      /* ---------- chapter 4: adjacency ---------- */
      {
        const el = document.getElementById("adjacency");
        const W = el.clientWidth, H = 320, M = { t: 16, r: 20, b: 34, l: 50 };
        const x = d3.scaleLinear(d3.extent(adjacency, (d) => d.density), [M.l, W - M.r]).nice();
        const y = d3.scaleLinear(d3.extent(adjacency, (d) => d.pci), [H - M.b, M.t]).nice();
        const r = d3.scaleSqrt(d3.extent(adjacency, (d) => d.world), [2, 14]);
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(5));
        svg.append("g").attr("class", "axis").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`).call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(6));
        svg.append("text").attr("x", W - M.r).attr("y", H - 6).attr("text-anchor", "end").attr("class", "annot").text("density → closer to Indonesia’s current strengths");
        svg.append("text").attr("x", M.l + 4).attr("y", M.t + 10).attr("class", "annot").text("↑ PCI (product sophistication)");
        const q80 = d3.quantile(adjacency.map((a) => a.density).sort(d3.ascending), 0.8);
        svg.selectAll("circle").data(adjacency).join("circle")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.density)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.pci)).attr("r", (d) => r(d.world))
          .attr("fill", (d) => (d.density > q80 && d.pci > 0) ? COPPER : SILVER)
          .attr("opacity", 0.55).attr("stroke", INK).attr("stroke-width", 0.5)
          .on("mousemove", function (e, d) {
            d3.select(this).attr("opacity", 1).attr("stroke", "#E6E8EC");
            showTip(e, `<b>${label(d.hs4)}</b><br>HS ${d.hs4}<br>density ${d.density.toFixed(2)} · PCI ${d.pci.toFixed(2)}<br>world trade ${fmt$(d.world * 1e3)}`);
          })
          .on("mouseleave", function () { d3.select(this).attr("opacity", 0.55).attr("stroke", INK); hideTip(); });
      }
    </script>

    <style is:global>
      html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body { margin: 0; }
      .stamp { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--accent); }
      .stamp.dim { color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }
      .copper { color: var(--accent); } .dim { color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .stamp-bar { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; z-index: 20; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 12px 20px; background: linear-gradient(color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 82%, transparent), transparent); pointer-events: none; }

      .hero { position: relative; height: 100vh; background: var(--ground); }
      #hero-canvas { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }
      .hero::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; background: linear-gradient(78deg, rgba(12,15,20,0.9) 0%, rgba(12,15,20,0.55) 34%, transparent 60%); }
      .hero-copy { position: absolute; left: 6vw; bottom: 12vh; max-width: 36rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; z-index: 2; }
      .hero-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4.2vw, 3rem); margin: 0; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
      .hero-copy p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 32rem; }

      .chapter { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 14vh 24px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
      .chapter h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0; }
      .chapter p { margin: 0; line-height: 1.65; }
      .big-stat { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.8vw, 1.7rem); line-height: 1.3; }
      .footnote { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .chart { width: 100%; } .chart.tall { min-height: 380px; }
      .axis { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 10px; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .axis path, .axis line { stroke: var(--hairline); }
      .annot { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 10px; fill: var(--ink-muted); letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
      .tm-name { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 11px; fill: #0C0F14; font-weight: 600; }
      .tm-pct { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 10px; fill: #0C0F14; }
      .scrub { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
      .scrub input, .controls input[type=range] { accent-color: var(--accent); width: 200px; }

      .explore { margin-top: 14vh; }
      .explore-head { max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px 16px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 32px; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; }
      .explore-head h2 { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 1.7rem; }
      .controls { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; align-items: center; }
      .toggle button { background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink-muted); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding: 7px 12px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; cursor: pointer; }
      .toggle button:first-child { border-radius: 4px 0 0 4px; }
      .toggle button:last-child { border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; border-left: 0; }
      .toggle button.on { background: var(--accent-ink); color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
      .search-wrap { position: relative; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
      #ps-search { width: 260px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); color: var(--ink); border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 12px; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.85rem; }
      #ps-results { position: absolute; top: 40px; left: 0; z-index: 8; width: 320px; background: var(--surface-raised); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden; }
      #ps-results button { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; width: 100%; text-align: left; background: none; border: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); color: var(--ink); padding: 8px 12px; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.8rem; cursor: pointer; }
      #ps-results button:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
      #ps-results button:hover { background: var(--accent-ink); }
      #ps-results button i { font-family: var(--font-data); font-style: normal; font-size: 0.62rem; color: var(--ink-muted); white-space: nowrap; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
      #search-status { min-height: 1em; }
      #ps-search:focus-visible, .toggle button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); }
      .ps-wrap { position: relative; height: 80vh; }
      #ps-canvas { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; cursor: grab; }
      #ps-canvas:active { cursor: grabbing; }
      #chart-tip { position: absolute; z-index: 30; pointer-events: none; background: var(--surface-raised); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px 11px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); }
      .cell { cursor: default; }
      #ps-tip { position: absolute; z-index: 5; pointer-events: none; background: var(--surface-raised); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px 11px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink); }
      .legend { position: absolute; left: 24px; bottom: 16px; }

      .method { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 12vh 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
      .method p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-muted); }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
